      "text": "Peds:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " children w microalbuminuria on repeat samples or persistently ↑BP (> 90th–95th percentile for age, or ≥ 130/80 mm Hg in adolescents) despite lifestyle chgs typically need an antiHTN, most often an ACEi or ARB; counsel pts of childbearing potential about ACEis, ARBs and statins."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
